📄 Final Report – 32-bit RISC Processor Design and Verification
1. Introduction & Objectives
Introduction:
The 32-bit RISC processor project demonstrates the design and verification of a Reduced Instruction Set Computer architecture. RISC processors are widely used due to their simplicity, efficiency, and scalability.

Objectives:

Implement a 32-bit RISC processor using Verilog HDL.

Verify functionality through simulation testbenches.

Document the design flow, results, and future improvements.
2. Processor Architecture Overview
Type: 32-bit RISC (Reduced Instruction Set Computer).

Word Size: 32 bits.

Registers:

32 General Purpose Registers (R0–R31).

Program Counter (PC).

Instruction Register (IR).

Pipeline Stages:

Instruction Fetch (IF).

Instruction Decode (ID).

Execute (EX).

Memory Access (MEM).

Write Back (WB).
3. Instruction Set & Datapath
Instruction Formats:

R-type: Register operations (ADD, SUB, AND, OR, SLT).

I-type: Immediate, load/store, branch (ADDI, LW, SW, BEQ).

J-type: Jump instructions (J, JAL).

Datapath Components:

Instruction Memory.

Register File.

ALU.

Data Memory.

Multiplexers (MUXes).

Control Unit.

Control Signals:

RegDst, ALUSrc, MemtoReg, RegWrite, MemRead, MemWrite, Branch, Jump, ALUOp.4. RTL Design (with Code Snippets)
Modules Implemented:

alu.v – Arithmetic and logical operations.

register_file.v – 32 registers with read/write ports.

control_unit.v – Opcode decoding and control signal generation.

datapath.v – Integration of ALU, Register File, Control Unit.

risc_processor.v – Top-level processor with PC and instruction memory.

Sample Code Snippet (ALU):
always @(*) begin
    case (alu_control)
        4'b0000: result = a & b;   // AND
        4'b0001: result = a | b;   // OR
        4'b0010: result = a + b;   // ADD
        4'b0110: result = a - b;   // SUB
        4'b0111: result = (a < b) ? 1 : 0; // SLT
        default: result = 0;
    endcase
end
Verification Results (with Waveform Screenshots)
Testbenches:

alu_tb.v – Verified AND, OR, ADD, SUB, SLT.

processor_tb.v – Verified PC reset, PC increment, instruction fetch, ALU results.

