Summary:

All modules passed functional verification.

Outputs matched expected theoretical values.

Design ready for extension (pipeline stages, hazard handling).

6. Conclusion & Future Work
Conclusion:
The 32-bit RISC processor was successfully designed, implemented, and verified. The modular design ensures clarity and scalability.

Future Work:

Add pipeline registers for full 5-stage pipeline implementation.

Implement hazard detection and forwarding
Extend instruction set (multiplication, division, shift operations).

Integrate cache memory for performance improvement.

Explore FPGA implementation for hardware validation.
